+/// Make this shape crushable: each of its contacts pushes with at most maxForce (newtons), shared between the
+/// contact's points, so a body meeting something rigid decelerates over a distance instead of stopping within a
+/// step. The limit of a contact is the smaller of its two shapes' limits, and it may change every step.
+/// A plastic contact gets no push-out and no restitution: the overlap it reaches is kept, as a crushed part keeps
+/// its shape. A contact that is not plastic keeps the usual soft push-out and restitution, within the limit.
+/// Crushable contacts are solved in the overflow color, on the scalar path. A maxForce of zero or less makes the
+/// shape rigid again.
+/// Contacts are kept, with their warm starting, when a shape becomes crushable or rigid.
+B3_API void b3Shape_SetCrushLimit( b3ShapeId shapeId, float maxForce, bool plastic );
+
+/// The shape's crush limit in newtons, or zero when the shape is rigid.
+B3_API float b3Shape_GetCrushLimit( b3ShapeId shapeId );
+
+/// Is the shape's crush limit plastic?
